{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0EUK", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a8e067d4be5586a393e086c1840522f4e622ff65fff9239db85e7ec79e698693", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext we define seminormal schemes and absolutely weakly normal schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:58f50b636cefa7b161afed0ae3f8fe4b8895ecf61584364d9674ef358dcc32f0", "unit_id": "tag:0EUK:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0EUK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(R) = U \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$R$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Spec(R) = U \\subset X$", "MATH_0009": "$R$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-seminormal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:27057bf0dd5e6c423626fe11161ad3643e1ac55cb4d03e2135cb00d67367f45b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:45a7a4b00ad4f78d844476baa6035cc97fa3078bcc90b0c76c73083f690d98ec", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>seminormal<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if every <MATH_0003> has\nan affine open neighbourhood <MATH_0004>\nsuch that the ring <MATH_0005> is seminormal.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0006> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>absolutely weakly normal<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if every <MATH_0007> has\nan affine open neighbourhood <MATH_0008>\nsuch that the ring <MATH_0009> is absolutely weakly normal.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8372c7a8eeda61f5bd631b92be212f2e5a22060454a8187361b9b2b257ac2248", "unit_id": "tag:0EUN:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0EUK", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a8e067d4be5586a393e086c1840522f4e622ff65fff9239db85e7ec79e698693", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the obligatory lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:99d1a0dd498ee2a8b0a2f67d661ab75d45f401d0f5a9388b211f467773344032", "unit_id": "tag:0EUK:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0EUK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0008": "$X_j$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-seminormal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:555b2b125c46a99a2b385a173afe2abdca090cb0d8ed322725f9e75886cb4b24", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:26e5f4dc8e3173052b65ac6ce7acf33a839d256b1421db1c6031a193c017e28d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0002> is seminormal.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0003> the ring <MATH_0004>\nis seminormal.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0005> such that\neach <MATH_0006> is seminormal.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an open covering <MATH_0007>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0008> is seminormal.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0009> is seminormal\nthen every open subscheme is seminormal.\nThe same statements are true with ``seminormal'' replaced by\n``absolutely weakly normal''.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d7dfa735c6ba729c5b91799727ea1aeae15eec48579410d498ed02b0d45fbe98", "unit_id": "tag:0EUP:statement"}
